{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks","id":626792,"title":"Multipule Attacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-14T12:25:55-07:00","id":626792,"title":"Multipule Attacks","content":"Maybe I misunderstood but werewolves in Urshal and Garou have both claw and bite damage and it was my impression that they could do all three to the same target each round. This is what really made them combat monsters. Was I wrong? Do they only get one of the three each round?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:33:49-07:00","id":626816,"title":"","content":"They can only do one. Though, they can initiate a grapple through biting - They can still only do one attack per turn.<br /> <br /> They're 'combat monsters' largely due to the attribute bonuses, natural weapons and other abilities that each of their various forms give them, as well as their natural regeneration, a large amount of gifts and merits with combat focus, and a variety of other factors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 08-14-2015, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:24:27-07:00","id":626906,"title":"","content":"No multiple attacks on 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:40:14-07:00","id":626935,"title":"","content":"The Storytelling System doesn't handle multiple attacks in one round well, on top of the general issues with trying to work them into a tabletop game. It's too much of a force multiplier, when the simplest measure of ease or difficulty is meant to be dice bonuses, to just throw the entire pool again. Even in first edition, which had an occasional multiple attack Fighting Style maneuver, no, the Uratha forms didn't confer multiple attacks. It's almost always one attack to a round, even if that attack roll narratively represents a fast barrage of swipes or something rather than a single bite or slash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:58:00-07:00","id":626951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=626906#post626906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No multiple attacks on 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there is at least one exception in the form of autofire, plus some of the Fighting Styles from the Hurt Locker draft, though we'll see if any of them make it to print. In any case, the exceptions only allow you to attack multiple different opponents, never to attack the same target multiple times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:01:38-07:00","id":626956,"title":"","content":"Also the fifth dot of Werewolf's Relentless Assault fighting style, where upon filling a target with lethal or aggravated damage, with the same turn you can then attack another character within reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:57:27-07:00","id":626994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=626956#post626956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the fifth dot of Werewolf's Relentless Assault fighting style, where upon filling a target with lethal or aggravated damage, with the same turn you can then attack another character within reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah! I forgot about that one. Point being, multiple attacks are sometimes allowed in 2e, but only against separate targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:13:32-07:00","id":627029,"title":"","content":"And only sparsely handled.<br /> <br /> But one thing I think could be done indeed, to represent a barrage of fangs and claws, is a fighting Merit for creatures with multiple natural weapons to gain a bonus on the attack when feasible to use all of them. Maybe just extra dice in an All-Out would be suffice, but on a narrative POV it is kinda boring indeed for the arsenal of an Uratha to have no impact. Most of the time you just bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T21:26:10-07:00","id":627225,"title":"","content":"It does make for a disappointing image, though it would make combat last longer. The last major opponent (with minions) I threw at the pack didn't last two rounds once the Rahu got ahold of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T23:02:05-07:00","id":627291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks#post626792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I misunderstood but werewolves in Urshal and Garou have both claw and bite damage and it was my impression that they could do all three to the same target each round. This is what really made them combat monsters. Was I wrong? Do they only get one of the three each round?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not wargaming, nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T23:03:52-07:00","id":627292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=626906#post626906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No multiple attacks on 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Ever.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Warpath, fifth dot in Relentless Assault cackles in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T00:26:05-07:00","id":627350,"title":"","content":"If you think about it, the claws at least should have been obvious. If two claws = two attacks, <i>everyone</i> would get two attacks per round because humans have two fists. <br /> <br /> Hell, we've got feet too. Four attacks? It gets silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:07:01-07:00","id":627805,"title":"","content":"But the furious barrage of claws and fangs is still a trope for werewolves. Some suggestion about how to make them a thing in the game without two attacks as default, and without two attacks at the same target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:07:23-07:00","id":627903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=627805#post627805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the furious barrage of claws and fangs is still a trope for werewolves. Some suggestion about how to make them a thing in the game without two attacks as default, and without two attacks at the same target?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All-out attack? A furious barrage of claws and fangs with no regard for defense. Add Relentless Assault and things like Butchery for more multiple attacks per round fun, within the system.<br /> <br /> Multiple attacks per round on the same target can easily be handled as bonus dice on your attack roll with the fluff that you hit more than once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 08-15-2015, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:15:43-07:00","id":627911,"title":"","content":"Have you ever seen how a bear mauls its target? It uses both claws and its teeth. It could be considered grappling only with the claws digging in to cause more damage each round, do the new combat rules cover this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:17:06-07:00","id":628021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=627805#post627805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the furious barrage of claws and fangs is still a trope for werewolves. Some suggestion about how to make them a thing in the game without two attacks as default, and without two attacks at the same target?</div> </div> </div> </div>A furious barrage of attacks is a trope for a lot of things, and that's reflected by narratives and/or mechanics other than rerolling your entire dicepool multiple times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:24:57-07:00","id":628031,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's like standard operating procedure. An attack takes 3 seconds because it represents about 3 seconds worth of trying to hurt the other guy. It's not one swipe of a claw or one punch by any stretch of the imagination. <br /> <br /> Plus, werewolves can establish a grapple with a claw attack or a bite. That seems to model the whole brutal extended mauling thing pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:25:29-07:00","id":628033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=627911#post627911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever seen how a bear mauls its target? It uses both claws and its teeth. It could be considered grappling only with the claws digging in to cause more damage each round, do the new combat rules cover this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fact that you can initiate a grapple with a bite sort of reflects that, as you can render your enemy helpless as you maul them, essentially.<br /> <br /> Also just remember that any damage you do is nondescript. You can describe it however you want, so if you want to emphasize the savagery of werewolves, that's entirely and easily a thing your can do in your descriptions of the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T17:35:36-07:00","id":629277,"title":"","content":"If you get an exceptional success on a grappling check, even on the initiation, you get to choose an additional option from the list of grapple maneuvers. Choose damage twice, flavor it as claws+teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T17:51:55-07:00","id":629321,"title":"","content":"You could just describe an attack as clawing and gnawing at the same time. A rolled attack isn't necessarily 'a punch,' or a single blow. You wouldn't get double damage or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T00:13:54-07:00","id":629636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=629277#post629277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you get an exceptional success on a grappling check, even on the initiation, you get to choose an additional option from the list of grapple maneuvers. Choose damage twice, flavor it as claws+teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still pretty unclear if this is allowed or not. As written it's pretty ambiguous and AFAIK there's never been any official answer on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T00:36:20-07:00","id":629669,"title":"","content":"Does bonus damage from claws/bite count towards successes needed to achieve the exceptional success? In other words, would I only need three success if my PC establishes a grapple with a claw attack with damage rating of 2 for a total of 5 successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T02:57:52-07:00","id":629772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=629277#post629277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you get an exceptional success on a grappling check, even on the initiation, you get to choose an additional option from the list of grapple maneuvers. Choose damage twice, flavor it as claws+teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>An exceptional success on the initial roll gets you <i>one </i>manoeuvre. And two manoeuvres means two different ones anyway. Although werewolves can attack and grapple in the same turn so you can get two goes at damage that way I think. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beltrajor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does bonus damage from claws/bite count towards successes needed to achieve the exceptional success? In other words, would I only need three success if my PC establishes a grapple with a claw attack with damage rating of 2 for a total of 5 successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The bonus damage is just that - damage. Not successes. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T03:00:37-07:00","id":629775,"title":"","content":"Weapons bonuses (including from natural weapons like claws) don't count towards exceptional successes by my reading of it. They're applied after the roll is made, which means after you know if it was an exceptional success or not. A failed roll with a 2 Damage weapon doesn't turn a failure into a success with 2 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:10:07-07:00","id":629834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beltrajor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=629669#post629669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does bonus damage from claws/bite count towards successes needed to achieve the exceptional success? In other words, would I only need three success if my PC establishes a grapple with a claw attack with damage rating of 2 for a total of 5 successes?</div> </div> </div> </div> To quote the rules book - &quot;Exceptional Success: Your character\u2019s action succeeds beyond her expectations. Achieved by <u><i><b>rolling </b></i></u>five or more successes.&quot; Emphasis mine. It has to be done through the roll, not with bonus successes from any source.<br /> <br /> Also relevant: establishing a grapple. If you're using the &quot;grapple on top of doing damage&quot; effect of Gauru, Urhan, and Urshul, then the claws apply to doing damage as normal, you still need to hit for either damage or grapple. If you establish a grapple the old way, you cannot use claws as a bonus - they do not have the grapple property (only chains and rope do, though its an ST call if other weapons - including claws - should). Further, even if you do use a weapon with the grapple property, you only add the weapon rating as bonus dice, not bonus successes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:32:33-07:00","id":629848,"title":"","content":"Ok. Anyway through favored form 1 you can get brawl based rolls to get exceptional success with 3 die. Pretty good indeed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:35:21-07:00","id":629850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=629636#post629636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still pretty unclear if this is allowed or not. As written it's pretty ambiguous and AFAIK there's never been any official answer on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken, but it's better to rule one weird edge case of the combat rules that hasn't been officially answered rather than go against the tacit rule against implementing multiple attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T07:14:24-07:00","id":629887,"title":"","content":"In no way I'm going against the rules prohibiting multiple attacks, but I wonder of possibilities for making the claws of a werewolf be worth something. Y'know, by RAW you'll hardly have any reason to declare a claw attack if you can make a bite one. They got differentiated natural weapons, but one is simply better than the other. This is kinda weird and boring. An easier time for werewolves to do a barrage of attacks would be interesting, even I agreeing that description alone can accomplish that, but better distinction between weapons to make claws worth something is another issue. For now only Dalu Form have any reason to use claws at all, and just until it achieves a grapple.<br /> <br /> By the way, I wouldn't use double damage for grappling either, tough I could rule using the second Maneuver to add the damage rating of both natural weapons to the damage instead of just one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T08:43:09-07:00","id":629968,"title":"","content":"Teeth and claws in gauru are completely identical. There's no real need to specify unless you're using certain gifts, which generally necessitate claws, or if you're fighting a vampire or cannibalising someone for essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T08:50:13-07:00","id":629973,"title":"","content":"I wanted to do bashing damage at one point so I used claws but as a sort of backhand, you may not always want to do the maximum amount of damage possible. In addition there's things you aren't going to want to bite, like Elfive mentioned vampires and there's others like the Zmai, or pretty much anything if you have the taste-of-blood trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:04:41-07:00","id":629977,"title":"","content":"Yeah, also anything with the Venomous Ichor Dread Power (where biting would leave you poisoned). Tasting human blood is a kuruth trigger for some Uratha. If you're trying to tear a wall down, generally your claws will be more useful, though there is no mechanical basis for that.<br /> <br /> Claws have their uses. One of my characters tends to use claws only during combat with uratha or humans because her family has a reputation for cannibalism, so there can be RP reasons as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:10:06-07:00","id":629999,"title":"","content":"Some things you just do not want to bite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:39:34-07:00","id":630026,"title":"","content":"First, a vampire you WANT to bite.<br /> <br /> One of the specific benefits of biting is that it guarantees Lethal against things that can downgrade Lethal to Bashing.<br /> <br /> Gauru makes no distinction. All other forms do. Dalu can only bite on a grapple, so it isn't an option, it is a statement to use your claws. Urshul makes bite more powerful. Urhan not even give you the option for claw (but it just make sense). Using claws as bashing with backhands is just improvising rules, by RAW if you avoided clawing, well, you didn't used the claws to begin with (and I would make it simply unarmed).<br /> <br /> You can have RP reasons to not use your bite, and some very specific reasons, also. But it is all based on exception cases. The problem (not a huge one, indeed, but the one in discussion for now) is that there are no advantages whatsoever on using claws from a mechanical standpoint outside exceptional situations. They aren't a true mechanical option. Bite is simply superior in every regard except on the rare cases where you don't want to bite something.<br /> <br /> It is even weirder when you think that claws have both more maneuverability and reach from a descriptive POV. That is, the most versatile direct weapon in the werewolf arsenal is simply a bad choice relegated to the role of side-weapon for things you don't want to bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:49:09-07:00","id":630029,"title":"","content":"Maybe it is a style thing?<br /> <br /> In Gauru -<ul><li>In Werewolf on Werewolf fights, I tend to use Claws...</li> <li>In Werewolf on Human Fights, I tend to use Claws...</li> <li>In Werewolf on Spirit Fights, I tend to use Claws...</li> <li>Against Vampires, it varies...</li> </ul>In Urshul - I tend to use Bite.<br /> <br /> Yes, you want to bite SOME things, but by no means is it a necessity or requirement.<br /> If you want to use your voice while you fight (you know, like giving orders and coordinating attacks, etc), it kind of precludes Biting things. *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 08-17-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:55:47-07:00","id":630033,"title":"","content":"The reason you don't want to bite a vampire is because you can be afflicted by blood bonding, making you more susceptible to its disciplines.<br /> <br /> But yes, 'it is all based on exception cases,' as everything is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2015, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T11:38:03-07:00","id":630099,"title":"","content":"Using teeth on vampire:<br /> <br /> Pros: Does lethal (claws only do bashing)<br /> <br /> Cons: Risk of ingesting vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T12:26:37-07:00","id":630147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beltrajor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=629848#post629848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Anyway through favored form 1 you can get brawl based rolls to get exceptional success with 3 die. Pretty good indeed!</div> </div> </div> </div>What I don't get about this is... if 3 successes = 5; OR if 3 successes are still 3, but you apply the exceptional success effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T12:47:38-07:00","id":630155,"title":"","content":"In that case - Exceptional Success is 3 successes on the roll (rather than the normal 5), only the <i><b>threshold </b></i>for achieving Exceptional Success has been altered/reduced, and you can apply the Exceptional Success effects; it does not grant you extra successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T02:43:32-07:00","id":630888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=630147#post630147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I don't get about this is... if 3 successes = 5; OR if 3 successes are still 3, but you apply the exceptional success effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 Sucesses keep being 3 Successes but you get the effect asociated with an Exceptional Success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:19:45-07:00","id":631004,"title":"","content":"It's still unclear to me that it you achieve a grapple, but not through exceptional success, when does the next step (contested roll and winner chooses manouver) takes place? Next turn? Inmediately after the grapple is established? In opponent's initiative step if it has yet to come? Thanks to anyone enlightens me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:28:49-07:00","id":631012,"title":"","content":"It's next turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-18-2015, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:36:16-07:00","id":631058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=631012#post631012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if someone at Initiative 12 grappled somebody at Initiative 10, then the character at Initiative 10 doesn't get to do anything until the order swings back around to 12, and then they have to do the opposed Grapple check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:51:41-07:00","id":631310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=630888#post630888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3 Sucesses keep being 3 Successes but you get the effect asociated with an Exceptional Success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got a source there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:07:43-07:00","id":631317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=631310#post631310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got a source there?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Choose a Physical Skill. When using that Skill in the favored form, exceptional successes occur on three successes instead of five.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:25:40-07:00","id":631334,"title":"","content":"Still vaguely written. Could mean either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:29:02-07:00","id":631337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=631334#post631334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still vaguely written. Could mean either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not vague in the slightest. Why would you think that 3 successes somehow becomes 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:33:20-07:00","id":631342,"title":"","content":"That is possibly the least vague sentence I have ever read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:27:22-07:00","id":631489,"title":"","content":"Given hat he game is very clear about what is an Exceptional Success and what is the number of successes, how could 3 become 5?<br /> <br /> Of course it doesn't directly state that 3 is 3. It doesn't give any reason to think otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:36:45-07:00","id":631657,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, an Exceptional Success is a specific effect of the rules that gives and extra advantage <i>on top of that of your Successes </i>however much they be. Default rule is you need to score 5, some rules allow you to get it on 3.<br /> <br /> Look at another example: Leg Wrack needs a quantity Bashing damage equal to the Stamina to be applied, on top of targeting the leg. The Urshul ability lets you apply that Tilt on an attack even if you don't use a targeted attack. Would you rule that such an attack would <i>at least</i> do (Target's Stamina) Bashing damage to (to a vampire, for example that would receive that kind of damage from a claw attack) because of the wording of the Tilt, and the fact that the Urshul ability doesn't specify otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T16:46:43-07:00","id":631719,"title":"","content":"In addition, hah, if an ability allows you to add successes, it says so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T15:23:51-07:00","id":632785,"title":"","content":"When a rule allows you to score an exceptional success on 3 instead of 5, you still only have the number of successes you originally rolled. You don't get additional successes to raise you up to the level of a standard exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T18:44:57-07:00","id":632943,"title":"","content":"Ok, I don't know much about the crunch of either edition, but I figured my ideas were worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> If you want to deal non-trivial damage to multiple opponents (the aforementioned furious barrage), you use claws, because your arms are longer than your neck. Let's say there is a 4 or 5 dot Merit that requires Primal Urge 4 and Brawl 3. After you add successes and damage bonus together, this Merit allows you to multiply that result by 3. This new total damage can be distributed among your opponents. This requires you to make an All-Out Attack, therefore sacrificing your Defense to represent the wild abandon and disregard for your safety. Any other Merits or powers that increase the standard +2 bonus granted by an All-Out Attack apply here as well. However, each opponent cannot receive more damage than the sum of your successes and damage bonus.<br /> <br /> Example: suppose your werewolf is in Gauru form and decides to use this Merit. He rolls Strength + Brawl + 5, gets 5 successes and his claws have a damage bonus of +2L. The total damage is 7, and after we multiply it by 3, it becomes 21. If he has three opponents, he may divide the damage equally to deal 7 lethal to each one. However, he could not deal 1 lethal to two opponents and then deal 19 lethal to the third opponent. Assuming the Beaten Down Tilt can be applied to them, they probably give up the fight immediately and do what you tell them to. This Merit doesn't let you defeat crowds in one turn and is not as useful against other werewolves (or most monsters). But it is better than not having the option. You may adjust the precise dot rating of this Merit and its prerequisites if you wish.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the +3 bonus to Strength inherent to the Gauru form is already significant. Despite that, you might determine that initiating a grapple with fangs while in this form also benefits from 9 Again. This means that a werewolf in Gauru form who decides to make an All-Out Attack, initiate grappling with teeth and spend Willpower gets +8 and 9 Again. He may proceed with mauling the victim as usual, with an Exceptional Success on this super grappling roll allowing you to choose the standard overpowering maneuvers. If you add that Merit which makes Exceptional Success in a grapple require 3 successes instead of 5, the kill becomes even quicker. A high Defense and extremely tough Armor might decrease the effectiveness of this super grapple roll. You might create another Merit with a Primal Urge X and/or Brawl X prerequisite that upgrades the grappling bonus of Gauru fangs from 9 Again to 8 Again.<br /> <br /> Does all of this sound reasonable? Keep in mind that this is mostly for dealing with multiple opponents at once, or vastly increasing your chance of killing almost anything you manage to grapple. Opponents that are werewolves or high Rank spirits are not so easily defeated. Heck, most monsters with lots of Defense, Armor, healing factors and miscellaneous protective measures are not guaranteed kills either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-19-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T19:07:39-07:00","id":632953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=632943#post632943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does all of this sound reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's way, way overpowered. Just multiplying successes by 2 would be ridiculously overpowered.<br /> <br /> If you wanna deal with multiple opponents at once, you roll Down &amp; Dirty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T19:28:38-07:00","id":632962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=632953#post632953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. That's way, way overpowered. Just multiplying successes by 2 would be ridiculously overpowered.<br /> <br /> If you wanna deal with multiple opponents at once, you roll Down &amp; Dirty.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, dammit, I forgot about Down &amp; Dirty. Looking at the relevant page again, Gauru form forces combat to use Down &amp; Dirty in 2ed if the opponents are regular humans/animals or weak spirits. Heck, the Defense that is subtracted from your dice pool in this case doesn't even include Athletics.<br /> <br /> This goes to show how an idea is often better in the imagination.<br /> <br /> But what about giving 9 or 8 Again to grapple rolls with Gauru fangs? Is that overpowered too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T20:03:44-07:00","id":632980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/626792-multipule-attacks?p=632962#post632962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, dammit, I forgot about Down &amp; Dirty. Looking at the relevant page again, Gauru form forces combat to use Down &amp; Dirty in 2ed if the opponents are regular humans/animals or weak spirits. Heck, the Defense that is subtracted from your dice pool in this case doesn't even include Athletics.<br /> <br /> This goes to show how an idea is often better in the imagination.<br /> <br /> But what about giving 9 or 8 Again to grapple rolls with Gauru fangs? Is that overpowered too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the Rahu already have 8 again on all Brawl dice pools with Killer Instinct.<br /> <br /> Edit: And Weaponry dice pools if you are wondering <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Edit2: I am not sure what are you trying to achieve with this merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 08-19-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T08:32:17-07:00","id":633501,"title":"","content":"Well, there's the level 5 from relentless assault fighting style, but as it forces you to basu-im I'd say it's certainly not something to be taken lightly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}